# 5-Stage Pipelined RISC-V RV32I Processor in Verilog

A 5-stage pipelined RISC-V RV32I processor implemented in pure Verilog-2001.
The design includes forwarding, hazard detection, load-use stall, and branch
flush. Verified with a directed testbench.

## Architecture

5-stage pipeline:

| Stage | Name | Function |
|-------|------|----------|
| **IF** | Instruction Fetch | Fetches instruction from instruction memory |
| **ID** | Instruction Decode | Decodes instruction, reads registers, generates immediate |
| **EX** | Execute | ALU operations, branch resolution, forwarding muxes |
| **MEM** | Memory Access | Load/store data memory |
| **WB** | Write Back | Writes result back to register file |

## Hazard Handling

| Hazard Type | Solution |
|-------------|----------|
| **Data hazard (RAW)** | Forwarding unit (EX/MEM → EX, MEM/WB → EX) |
| **Load-use hazard** | Hazard detection unit inserts 1-cycle stall |
| **Control hazard** | Branch flush (IF/ID and ID/EX cleared) |

## File Structure
5-stage-pipelined-RISC-V-RV32I-processor-in-Verilog/
├── rtl/
│ ├── rv32i_core.v # Top-level core
│ ├── if_stage.v # Instruction Fetch
│ ├── id_stage.v # Instruction Decode
│ ├── ex_stage.v # Execute
│ ├── mem_stage.v # Memory Access
│ ├── wb_stage.v # Write Back
│ ├── hazard_unit.v # Load-use hazard detection
│ └── forwarding_unit.v # Data forwarding logic
├── tb/
│ └── tb_rv32i.v # Testbench
├── sim/
│ └── run.f # Run file
└── README.md

text

## Supported Instructions

| Type | Instructions |
|------|-------------|
| **R-type** | ADD, SUB, AND, OR, XOR, SLL, SRL, SLT, SLTU |
| **I-type** | ADDI, ANDI, ORI, XORI, SLTI, SLTIU, SLLI, SRLI |
| **Load** | LB, LH, LW, LBU, LHU |
| **Store** | SB, SH, SW |
| **Branch** | BEQ, BNE, BLT, BGE, BLTU, BGEU |
| **Jump** | JAL, JALR |
| **Upper** | LUI, AUIPC |

## How to Run

### Option A: EDA Playground

1. Login at [edaplayground.com](https://edaplayground.com)
2. Select **Icarus Verilog** or **Aldec Riviera Pro**
3. Paste all `rtl/*.v` files → **Design** box
4. Paste `tb/tb_rv32i.v` → **Testbench** box
5. Run

### Option B: Icarus Verilog (Local)

```bash
cd sim
iverilog -o rv32i_sim ../rtl/*.v ../tb/tb_rv32i.v
vvp rv32i_sim
Option C: Verilator (Local)
bash
verilator --binary -j 0 --top-module tb_rv32i \
    rtl/*.v tb/tb_rv32i.v
./obj_dir/Vtb_rv32i
Expected Output
text
========================================
RV32I 5-Stage Pipelined Processor Test
========================================
